WHY ALL-RIGHTS-RESERVED, AND WHAT IT IS WORTH

This is the conservative default, chosen because the intent is to sell this
plugin and because picking an open-source licence on someone's behalf is not
reversible - anything released under one stays released under it for that
version, forever. If a permissive licence is wanted later, it can be granted;
the other direction cannot.

It is also worth being clear about what a licence and a licence check actually
achieve here. The plugin ships as a .NET assembly, and a .NET assembly can be
decompiled and a check patched out. The licence check in this software raises
the cost of casual copying between servers; it is not DRM and cannot be made
into DRM. What this file provides is the legal position, which is the part that
is actually enforceable.
